{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":5,"timestamp":1791458064,"nonce":"TL3IkcQzUdAr41UY7x8VMotL4OU=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADORPa0Bs8AAAABV13nR88AAAAHoeM-1A"},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"timestamp":1791889163,"nonce":"cSr3Rd9tB0nKqyiIq3jNCf11GCw=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDORPa0Bs8AAAABbjbI3A","github-url":"https://github.com/FhG-IISB/jNO/issues/158#issuecomment-6144051420"},"message":"A related change landed on `feat/region-nodes` (63c5c4d) that this issue would make cheap.\n\n**What it does.** Region properties declared with `.attach(...)` and read as `d.\u003cprop\u003e` (e.g. `d.k`, `d.q`) are now leaves that read their value from the domain when the terms are lowered (`AttachedLiteral`, a `Literal` subclass). `domain.attach` counts changes per property, and a built `fem` re-assembles from its stored terms when a property it reads has changed:\n\n```python\nfem = jno.fem([d.k * (ui.x*vi.x + ui.y*vi.y) - d.q * vi, u(xb, yb) - 0.0])\nu1 = fem.solve()\nd.attach(\"heater\", q=2.0e6)\nu2 = fem.solve()      # INFO: jno.fem: re-assembled, since domain.attach changed 'q' ...\n```\n\nBefore, the second solve silently returned `u1`. The mesh and anything built on it (enclosure view factors) are not rebuilt; expression values (functions of position, `jno.fn`, trainable parameters) are captured as written and refuse to solve once re-attached.\n\n**Connection to this issue.** That re-assembly is a full rebuild, so it pays the recompile described above on every changed value — a parameter sweep over attached values is exactly the continuation pattern here. The `AttachedLiteral` leaves are a natural first target for literal hoisting: they are the values the user has said will change, they are already identified in the trace, and hoisting only them would avoid the structural-constant question (point 1) for every other literal. With them hoisted, the version check could pass the new values as program inputs instead of rebuilding.","files":null}]}